  "kind": "mnt.theme-pack",
  "packVersion": 2,
  "cssApiVersion": 1,
  "meta": {
    "name": "Quiet Icons",
    "description": "Website icons rest in grayscale and bloom into full colour on hover, with an accent halo on the focused search bar.",
    "notes": "Any calm, low-contrast wallpaper suits this; the effect is about icons, not the backdrop."
  },
  "theme": {
    "mode": "dark",
    "color": {
      "bg": "#102932",
      "surface": "#1d353d",
      "text": "#eeeae5",
      "accent": "#90d5cd"
    }
  },
  "css": ".mnt-link-icon {\n  filter: grayscale(1) opacity(0.75);\n  transition: filter var(--mnt-dur-base) var(--mnt-ease), box-shadow var(--mnt-dur-base) var(--mnt-ease);\n}\n.mnt-link:hover .mnt-link-icon,\n.mnt-link:focus-visible .mnt-link-icon {\n  filter: grayscale(0) opacity(1);\n}\n\n.mnt-search {\n  transition: border-color var(--mnt-dur-base) var(--mnt-ease), box-shadow var(--mnt-dur-base) var(--mnt-ease);\n}\n.mnt-search:focus-within {\n  border-color: var(--mnt-accent);\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--mnt-accent-soft), 0 8px 24px -12px var(--mnt-accent);\n}\n\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  .mnt-link-icon,\n  .mnt-search {\n    transition: none;\n  }\n}"
}
```

The idea is restraint: the page stays quiet and the colour lives only in the tinted icons, so a gentle grayscale at rest keeps the grid calm and the hover bloom feels like a small reward. The search bar's focused halo is the one place the accent is allowed to glow.

I'll add a weather widget and a starter todo list to your overview area, keeping your existing clock, search and bookmarks in place, with a soft teal palette matching what you already have.

```json
