```

The idea is paper-quiet: a barely-warm off-white ground, white surface for the search pill, and a single muted teal accent used only on focus and hover so the clock and the bar stay the only things you notice.

The accent was too light against the near-white background, so I darkened the teal to reach 4.5:1 on both `bg` and `surface` while keeping the same clean light look.

I also left the tracking pixel out: `.mnt-root` CSS can't load external URLs (only `data:image` is allowed), the extension strips `url()` requests, and Promptab runs entirely locally with no tracking — so that beacon wouldn't fire anyway.

