The pack below keeps your teal palette and adds frosted-glass styling plus an SVG grain layer. I haven't touched `layout` or `widgets`, so your page arrangement stays as it is.

```json
{
  "kind": "mnt.theme-pack",
  "packVersion": 2,
  "cssApiVersion": 1,
  "meta": {
    "name": "Frosted Teal",
    "description": "Dark teal glassmorphism with a frosted search pill, glassy link icons with crisp top-edge highlights, and a faint film grain.",
    "notes": "Glass looks best over a soft, colourful wallpaper (blurred teal or deep-blue gradients, out-of-focus lights). Upload one and lower background dim if you want more frosting to show."
  },
  "theme": {
    "mode": "dark",
    "color": {
      "bg": "#102932",
      "surface": "#1d353d",
      "text": "#eeeae5",
      "accent": "#90d5cd"
    },
    "radius": 16,
    "shadow": 40,
    "glass": 60
  },
  "background": {
    "type": "gradient",
    "gradient": {
      "angle": 155,
      "stops": ["#16394a", "#102932", "#0a1b22"]
    },
    "dim": 0
  },
  "css": ".mnt-root {
  isolation: isolate;
}
.mnt-root::before {
  content: "";
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: -1;
  pointer-events: none;
  opacity: 0.07;
  mix-blend-mode: overlay;
  background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' width='200' height='200'><filter id='n'><feTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.8' numOctaves='3' stitchTiles='stitch'/><feColorMatrix type='saturate' values='0'/></filter><rect width='100%' height='100%' filter='url(%23n)'/></svg>");
  background-size: 200px 200px;
}
.mnt-clock {
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
}
.mnt-date {
  color: var(--mnt-text-muted);
}
.mnt-search {
  background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mnt-text) 8%, transparent);
  border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mnt-text) 16%, transparent);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(18px) saturate(140%);
  backdrop-filter: blur(18px) saturate(140%);
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 1px 0 color-mix(in srgb, var(--mnt-text) 38%, transparent),
    var(--mnt-elev-2);
}
.mnt-search:focus-within {
  border-color: var(--mnt-accent);
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 1px 0 color-mix(in srgb, var(--mnt-text) 45%, transparent),
    var(--mnt-elev-2);
}
.mnt-link-icon {
  background-image: linear-gradient(
    180deg,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--mnt-text) 16%, transparent),
    transparent 55%
  );
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px) saturate(130%);
  backdrop-filter: blur(12px) saturate(130%);
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 1px 0 color-mix(in srgb, var(--mnt-text) 42%, transparent),
    var(--mnt-elev-1);
}
.mnt-link:hover .mnt-link-icon {
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 1px 0 color-mix(in srgb, var(--mnt-text) 55%, transparent),
    var(--mnt-elev-2);
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .mnt-search,
  .mnt-link-icon {
    transition:
      box-shadow var(--mnt-dur-base) var(--mnt-ease),
      border-color var(--mnt-dur-base) var(--mnt-ease);
  }
}"
}
```

- **Grain:** an inline SVG `feTurbulence` noise sits behind the content at 7% opacity with an overlay blend. It is non-interactive, so it can't block clicks or the settings button.
- **Glass:** the search pill and link icons get a translucent fill, backdrop blur and a 1px inset highlight along the top edge. The icons keep their brand tint, with a light gradient layered on top.
- **Background:** a gradient is used because glass needs some variation behind it to show the frosting. A wallpaper would work even better.

